            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0396" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg386"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/15194: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-07T16:00:00+07:00">December 7, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2339. In telegram December 3 from Loyang, Drumright reports as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Rumors of further recent clashes between Chungking and Communist troops
                            Northern Shensi denied by Vice Chief Staff [at] Loyang who states
                            Communists have recently reinforced their troops in that sector. He
                            categorically denies Chungking intends attacking <pb facs="0397" n="387"
                                xml:id="pg387"/> Communists at present. While admitting Communists
                            have formed in North China barrier against northward advance of
                            Chungking troops, he states puppet troops in the North under Chi
                            Hsieh-yuan (Peiping régime) and those in Kifeng region under Chang
                            Lan-feng (Nanking régime) will be used by Chungking to oppose
                            Communists. If Chungking-Communist clash should occur, he said, certain
                            Communist [<hi rendition="#italic">puppet?</hi>] units would support
                            Central Government.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
